  "takeaway": "Mesh-only extraction on Ours-full is operational on the main and thin-leaf samples. Smaller truncation reduces post-processed mesh vertices by about 12% on KongQueZhuYu and 11.5% on XianKeLai1, but it also increases connected components and boundary edges, so compactness may come with fragmentation risk. Post-boundary cleanup preserves component counts and remains conservative, with larger displacement on the thin-leaf sample. These are mesh-structure results only, not evidence of leaf-width or phenotype accuracy improvement.",
